==Post-match==
[[Pep Guardiola]], the winning manager, was elated: "It was an incredible final for us and we have finished an incredible year{{nbsp}}...  To all the people at the club a big congratulations, especially the players because they are the reason why we have won these titles".<ref name=guardlive/>  His opposite number, [[Javi Gracia]] said: "we knew before the game we had to play the perfect game{{nbsp}}...  We started well and we created the best chance after 10 minutes with Roberto Pereyra but after that they dominated.  They were better, congratulations to them and we will try again".<ref name=guardlive/>  De Bruyne was named as the [[player of the match|man of the match]].<ref name=guardlive/>  Kompany, the City captain, said: "As soon as we scored the two goals and they had to come at us and press{{nbsp}}...  It made it easier for us.  It wasn't as easy as the score suggests".<ref name=guardlive/>  The day after the game, Kompany said that the match was his final game for the club as he would be leaving after eleven years to become the [[player-manager]] of [[R.S.C. Anderlecht|Anderlecht]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Vincent Kompany leaves Manchester City to become Anderlecht player-manager |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/48325845 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=19 May 2019 |access-date=19 May 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190519081347/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/48325845 |archive-date=19 May 2019 |url-status=live }}</ref>  Watford's Gomes decided against retirement and instead signed a one-year extension to his contract.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/48805936 | title = Heurelho Gomes: Watford's veteran keeper signs new one-year | publisher=[[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 16 July 2020 | date = 28 June 2019 | archive-date = 9 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210309231412/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/48805936 | url-status = live }}</ref>

Daniel Taylor writing in ''[[The Guardian]]'' described the game as a "cakewalk" for City.<ref name=demo>{{Cite web | url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2019/may/18/manchester-city-win-treble-watford-fa-cup-final-match-report | work = [[The Guardian]] | title = Manchester City win FA Cup to seal treble with 6–0 demolition of Watford | first = Daniel | last = Taylor | access-date = 16 July 2020 | date = 18 May 2019 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20200301211541/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2019/may/18/manchester-city-win-treble-watford-fa-cup-final-match-report | archive-date = 1 March 2020 | url-status = live }}</ref>  City scored 26 goals during the season's cup campaign, the most by any FA Cup-winning team since the [[1925–26 FA Cup]].<ref name=rep11v11/> It was also the largest margin of victory in an FA Cup Final since the [[1903 FA Cup final|1903 final]] which ended with the same scoreline, [[Bury F.C.|Bury]] beating [[Derby County F.C.|Derby County]].<ref name=rep11v11/>  Manchester City became the first English men's team to win a domestic [[Treble (association football)|treble]], having already won the EFL Cup and Premier League that season.<ref>{{cite news |last=Bullin |first=Matt |date=18 May 2019 |title=Man City win treble – how impressive is that achievement? |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/48321358 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |access-date=18 May 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190518180734/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/48321358 |archive-date=18 May 2019 |url-status=live }}</ref> 

Winning the FA Cup meant that Manchester City qualified to play [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]], the Premier League runners-up, in the [[2019 FA Community Shield|Community Shield]] in August which they won on penalties after a 1–1 draw.<ref>{{cite news |date=4 August 2019 |title=Community Shield: Liverpool 1–1 Man City (City won 5–4 on penalties) |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/49141690 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |first = Emlyn | last= Begley | access-date=17 November 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190808212252/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/49141690 |archive-date=8 August 2019 |url-status=live }}</ref>  City's victory meant that Wolves went into the second qualifying round of the [[2019–20 UEFA Europa League]] having finished seventh in the Premier League while [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] went directly into the group stages.<ref name=guardlive3/>

